","inadequate communication of trial details",""],[7305,2813,"The Hospital notes for Mr. Adams admission on the 30","omission of critical complication details",""],[7737,2963,"The apparent abandoment of this lady in AMU.","abandonment of elderly patient in acute medical unit",""],[7738,2963,"The failure to record the timing and reason for the Doctor's visit (the reason was only illicited from evidence)","incomplete documentation of medical review",""],[7739,2963,"The failure to seek an early Senior Review for the failure to record the Fluid Chart correctly - this is important because it was fluid overload that was the immediate cause of Mrs. [name redacted] death","delayed senior review of fluid charting",""],[7740,2963,"Failure to act on the NEWS score and create a plan for Mrs. Woods and assist her","inadequate response to clinical deterioration",""],[7741,2963,"Failure to canulate her appropriately. Her cannula had initially been inserted by the ambulance crew, this tissued and needed to be replaced. The","inadequate intravenous access management",""],[8064,3078,"Delay in being seen both by Nursing Staff and Doctors in A & E. Delay in being seen by Surgical Team after referral to them at 05:30 hours on the 13\" July 2013. Delay in ongoing assessment by the Surgical Team when he started to deteriorate and no Surgical Team member was available to respond to the calls for help from the Nursing Staff at the Acute Medical Unit.","delayed medical assessment",""],[8066,3078,"Inappropriate transfer to an Acute Medical Unit when he should either have stayed in A & E or gone to a Surgical Unit. The concern was that he was effectively unsafe and in an inappropriate clinical environment.","inappropriate clinical environment",""],[8067,3078,"There was a failure to appreciate his deterioration largely because he was not seen by the Surgical Team in spite of requests that he should be seen.","failure to recognize deterioration",""],[8068,3078,"Even though his acute abdomen had 